Subject: [PATCH 22/41] MTROPOLIS: Add a hack swapping restored point lists for
 Uncle Albert's Fabulous Voyage

The original player stores the points of list variables as Y, X in the
variable files written by the Save and Restore modifier, and the game
swaps the coordinates of its object, plate and photo position lists back
after loading them. ScummVM saves keep points as they are, so the game's
swap put every notebook object of a resumed game at the wrong position.

When a Save and Restore modifier loads a ScummVM save, swap the
coordinates of the restored point lists for this game, so that they
reach the game the way the original files did. Variable files from the
game directory already load that way.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
